; OVERVIEW
; The upper half of bank 0: the continuation of P0-B0 (the image runs on from
; 3FFFH into 4000H without a break).  It holds the screen editor and line input,
; LIST/program-line storage, and the BASIC statement handlers that are not in
; bank 3: CLEAR, RESTORE, CURSOR, MODE, CLS, LINE, IF, RUN, GOTO, GOSUB, RETURN,
; FOR/NEXT, RETI, RESUME, DIM, ERASE, LET, READ, WAIT, PAUSE, STOP, END, USING,
; INKEY$, KBUFF$, KEYSTAT, LOCK/UNLOCK, BREAK, DELETE.  Routines of P0-B0 are
; called by name (see the equates); page 1 must be bank 0 while this code runs,
; which BANKJP/RST 18H with a C000H-FFFFH target or the P0-B0 trampolines ensure.
; ============================================================================

; ---- I/O ports ----
